  "body": "Depends on #1069 (drafted windows of several streams verified in one pass; this uses its lanes with row spans). The branch carries #1069's two commits (`3ced86d9`, `71fc0971`) under its own one (`5cc536ce`), so only the last commit is this change; I'll rebase once #1069 lands.\n\n## What this changes\n\nThe recipe's \"Not yet\" list says the MTP head drafts one stream at a time. With #1069 the verify windows of a round\nshare one pass, but the head still ran each stream's absorb pass and chain steps alone: on a GB10 at four streams a\nround spent ~29 ms in head passes, against ~5 ms at one stream (per-pass timing: a verify pass is ~42 ms + 2.6 ms a\nrow, the c=4 chat round 110 ms).\n\n- `facts()` sets `.draft_streams`, so the lanes core asks a shared round's drafts in one call (as Nemotron's and GLM's\n  backends do).\n- `draftBatched` takes the call's greedy streams (no trees, no media): rollbacks as before, then `Ops.draftMany`: each\n  stream's kept rows absorbed in one head pass (`forwardHeadMany`, a lane each on its own head cache and position),\n  then one pass a chain step for the streams still drafting, every active stream's best read in one download. Each\n  stream picks and stops by the same rule as alone (confidence, count, chain limit).\n- Every row of a batched head pass runs the ops a lone `forwardHead` runs on it (row-wise kernels, the per-lane\n  attention of #1069), so each stream gets exactly the drafts it gets alone.\n- Sampled streams, trees and media keep the one-at-a-time path. `TF_FLASHNEXT_BATCH_HEADS=0` restores it for every\n  stream; `TF_FLASHNEXT_DEPTH_LOG=1` prints each stream's chain length by round width every 200 calls.\n\n## Receipt\n\n- Environment: TensorFold `main` `d1018b31` + #1069 + this branch; one DGX Spark (GB10, sm_121, CUDA 13.0);\n  `nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local@b9ce18a6`, `TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_HEAD=affine4`, `--parallel 4 --context 40960`.\n  The numbers below were taken on a local stack that also carries #1143 and #1147 (prompt-side, no effect on decode).\n- Exactness: with the batched head and with `TF_FLASHNEXT_BATCH_HEADS=0` every request's rounds and accepted/drafted\n  counts are equal (four-stream chat: 100 rounds, 155/256 each; code: 56 rounds, 199/229), i.e. the same drafts;\n  `bench_concurrent.py --alone --serial`: concurrent == alone 4/4, drafted == `\"draft\": false` 1/1.\n- Decode speed (`bench_concurrent.py`, 256 tokens, greedy, aggregate tok/s):\n\n  | | one at a time | batched | |\n  | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n  | 4 streams, code | 130.2 | 150.7 | 1.16x |\n  | 4 streams, chat | 88.9 | 99.8 | 1.12x |\n  | 1 stream, code / chat | 70.7 / 44.2 | 70.7 / 44.3 | 1.00x |\n\n  The four-stream chat round falls from ~110 to ~98 ms.\n- Chain lengths at four streams (`TF_FLASHNEXT_DEPTH_LOG`, length: stream-rounds): 0:3 1:229 2:60 3:157 4:43 5:100\n  6:144.\n- Kernel contract: no kernel changes.\n- Tests run: `zig build test --summary all` (built `-Dnvcc`): 211/211 steps, 2,959 of 2,973 tests passed, 14 skipped.\n- Not run, and why: sampled streams (they keep the one-at-a-time path); two ranks.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- **Stacked on #1069:** the diff against `main` includes its commits until it merges.\n- **Greedy streams only:** sampled streams, trees and media still draft one at a time, so their speed is unchanged.\n- **Local stack:** the numbers were taken on a stack that also carries #1143 and #1147. Those are prompt-side, but this branch alone wasn't timed separately.\n- **Chat still trails vLLM MTP3 at four streams:** 99.8 against 104.8 tok/s. Code is ahead, at 150.7 against 108.6.\n- **Not run:** two ranks.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Every token still goes through the lane rounds. No serial path, and nothing that needs drafts off.\n- [x] Drafted output equals `\"draft\": false` (8/8), concurrent equals solo (8/8), and a resumed two-turn prompt equals a fresh one (7,147 of 7,184 tokens restored), each equal to `main`'s output (MTP drafts on, `--prompt-cache-gib 4`; measured at `5cc536ce`, before the later lean fix, which only folds comments and moves code). Each stream gets the same drafts as alone.\n- [x] No precision traded for speed. The bits do not change.\n- [x] No GPU kernel changes, so the kernel contract is unaffected.\n- [x] Prompt processing is unaffected (decode-only change).\n- [x] Platforms: CUDA on GB10 (sm_121), one rank. No Metal change.\n- [x] New tests: none needed beyond #1069's per-stream byte tests; the batched path is checked by equal rounds and accepted/drafted counts against `TF_FLASHNEXT_BATCH_HEADS=0`.\n- [x] Comments are one line. No measurements or history in the source.\n- [x] No personal data, machine names, internal hosts or local paths. No AI attribution lines.\n\n",
